<root>
  <h2>Animation perf stress (500 keyed items)</h2>
  <section>
    <p style="color:var(--fg-muted);font-size:0.875rem;margin:0 0 0.75rem">
      Mounts a <code>pine-tags-input-root</code> with up to 500 keyed
      <code>pine-tags-input-item</code> chips — each one a Pine
      compound with a <code>scale</code> mount transition and
      <code>flip</code> layout animation.
      <strong>Mount</strong> dumps all 500 at once (with
      <code>pp-stagger="2"</code> spacing the enters across ~1s).
      <strong>Simulate streamed load</strong> adds 10 chips every
      20&nbsp;ms — a realistic "data arriving in batches" flow that
      exercises the incremental-insert path (new keys stream in
      while existing ones stay put).
      <strong>Rotate</strong> moves the head to the tail (a
      minimal reorder); <strong>Shuffle</strong>
      Fisher-Yates-shuffles the whole list (every item moves). The
      last two report wall-clock time across the full reconcile
      (handler start → after reactive flush). Use these to spot
      regressions in the RFC-039 dispatch path or the pp-for
      reconcile.
    </p>
    <div class="row" style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">
      <pine-button @click="mount_fixture">
        <span pp-text="open ? 'Unmount stress fixture' : 'Mount 500-row stress fixture'"></span>
      </pine-button>
      <pine-button variant="ghost" @click="simulate_add" pp-show="!open">
        Simulate streamed load
      </pine-button>
      <pine-button variant="ghost" @click="rotate" pp-show="open">
        Rotate
      </pine-button>
      <pine-button variant="ghost" @click="shuffle" pp-show="open">
        Shuffle
      </pine-button>
      <span pp-show="open && last_op" style="font-size:0.875rem;align-self:center">
        last <strong pp-text="last_op"></strong>:
        <strong pp-text="shuffle_display"></strong>
      </span>
      <span pp-show="simulating" style="font-size:0.875rem;align-self:center;color:var(--fg-muted)">
        streaming… <strong pp-text="items.length"></strong> / 500
      </span>
    </div>
    <template pp-if="open">
      <pine-tags-input-root pp-model:values="items" class="tags-input-root">
        <template pp-for="item in items" pp-key="item" pp-stagger="2">
          <pine-tags-input-item :value="item">
            <pine-tags-input-item-text></pine-tags-input-item-text>
            <pine-tags-input-item-delete aria-label="Remove">×</pine-tags-input-item-delete>
          </pine-tags-input-item>
        </template>
      </pine-tags-input-root>
    </template>
  </section>
</root>
